# Project Glossary

## TTS (Text-to-Speech)
A technology that converts written text into spoken words using synthetic voices.

## Voice Cloning
The process of creating a digital replica of a person's voice, allowing for the generation of speech that sounds like the original speaker.

## Autoregressive Model
A type of model that generates data points in a sequence, where each point is dependent on its predecessors. In TTS, it predicts the next audio frame based on previous frames.

## Diffusion Model
A probabilistic model used to iteratively refine outputs, often employed in generating high-quality audio or images by progressively denoising a signal.

## Vocoder
A tool that converts spectral representations (like mel spectrograms) into audio waveforms, often used in TTS systems to produce natural-sounding speech from intermediate representations.

